# Record Shelf environment variables.
# Cloudflare Pages: set these in the dashboard / wrangler, not in a committed file.
# Docker / adapter-node: pass at runtime, e.g. `docker run -e ORIGIN=...`.

# adapter-node only: the public https origin the app is served from. Required for
# SvelteKit's CSRF/origin checks behind a proxy. e.g. https://records.example.com
# ORIGIN=https://localhost

# adapter-node only: port the node server listens on (default 3000).
# PORT=3000

# Who may write to the shared store (stored copies and value history). One or
# more token fingerprints, separated by commas or spaces. A fingerprint is the
# SHA-256 of a Discogs token: open /api/status with your token saved in Settings
# and copy the "fingerprint" value. It is one-way, so no token is kept on the
# server. Visitors whose token is not listed still see their own lists, loaded
# straight from Discogs and not stored. Unset: nothing is stored for anyone.
# Cloudflare Pages: add it as a secret named STORE_WRITERS.
# STORE_WRITERS=
